1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,740
At six-oh-two in the morning, my phone let out an alarm.

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:06,780
I woke up, reaching for it on the table.

3
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:09,590
The screen showed an emergency alert.

4
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:14,368
Residents were told to stay inside, lock their doors, and wait for the next update.

5
00:00:14,918 --> 00:00:16,745
I called a few numbers I knew.

6
00:00:17,095 --> 00:00:18,360
No one answered.

7
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:22,194
On the building's resident chat, messages kept jumping in.

8
00:00:22,544 --> 00:00:24,588
Someone asked what was happening.

9
00:00:24,938 --> 00:00:26,981
Someone said not to go outside.

10
00:00:27,331 --> 00:00:31,555
A video someone had just posted was deleted before I could finish watching it.

11
00:00:32,105 --> 00:00:33,498
I went to the window.

12
00:00:34,048 --> 00:00:36,818
Down on the street, a car rear-ended another.

13
00:00:37,168 --> 00:00:39,186
The driver abandoned it and ran.

14
00:00:39,536 --> 00:00:43,097
Near the corner store, a few people were struggling with each other.

15
00:00:43,447 --> 00:00:46,268
One of them fell, and the rest scattered fast.

16
00:00:46,818 --> 00:00:49,984
I pulled the curtain shut and went back to lock the door.

17
00:00:50,534 --> 00:00:52,092
I meant to stay inside.

18
00:00:52,642 --> 00:00:56,688
About ten minutes later, there was pounding on a door somewhere down the hallway.

19
00:00:57,038 --> 00:00:59,528
A man was calling for someone to let him in.

20
00:00:59,878 --> 00:01:02,253
I went closer and looked through the peephole.

21
00:01:02,803 --> 00:01:07,665
He was standing in front of the apartment across from mine, one hand holding the other arm.

22
00:01:08,015 --> 00:01:10,058
Blood was dripping onto the floor.

23
00:01:10,608 --> 00:01:13,787
Before I could do anything, the stairwell door burst open.

24
00:01:14,337 --> 00:01:15,755
Someone came out.

25
00:01:16,105 --> 00:01:17,179
Then another.

26
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:21,966
The man turned, pressed himself against the door, and started pounding harder.

27
00:01:22,516 --> 00:01:25,605
I pulled back from the peephole when the screaming started.

28
00:01:26,155 --> 00:01:29,703
Standing in the middle of the room, I heard thuds out in the hallway.

29
00:01:30,053 --> 00:01:33,002
A moment later, someone touched my own door handle.

30
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:35,914
The handle dipped, then sprang back up.

31
00:01:36,464 --> 00:01:38,048
I backed into the kitchen.

32
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:41,981
The apartment had a back door that led to a service stairwell.

33
00:01:42,331 --> 00:01:45,203
I had never used it except to take out the trash.

34
00:01:45,553 --> 00:01:51,997
I grabbed my backpack, put in two bottles of water, a few snack bars still in the cupboard, and the flashlight by the bed.

35
00:01:52,547 --> 00:01:54,667
There was no time to message anyone.

36
00:01:55,217 --> 00:01:57,898
Outside the front door, there was movement again.

37
00:01:58,448 --> 00:02:02,060
I went out through the back, and pulled it shut as quietly as I could.

38
00:02:02,610 --> 00:02:05,903
The service stairwell led down to an alley behind the building.

39
00:02:06,453 --> 00:02:08,037
There were people there too.

40
00:02:08,387 --> 00:02:11,234
A couple was helping an old woman into a car.

41
00:02:11,584 --> 00:02:16,254
The man told me to avoid the main road, there had been an accident at the intersection.

42
00:02:16,804 --> 00:02:18,414
I asked where I should go.

43
00:02:18,964 --> 00:02:20,931
He pointed toward the shopping mall.

44
00:02:21,481 --> 00:02:23,498
"They're letting people in over there."

45
00:02:24,048 --> 00:02:25,314
I went that way.

46
00:02:25,864 --> 00:02:28,761
From a distance, I could see the lights were still on.

47
00:02:29,111 --> 00:02:32,660
A security guard stood at the door, waving people inside.

48
00:02:33,010 --> 00:02:39,772
After what had just happened outside my apartment, just seeing someone in uniform still doing their job was enough to make me feel lighter.

49
00:02:40,322 --> 00:02:43,361
Inside, it was crowded, but not yet chaotic.

50
00:02:43,711 --> 00:02:45,575
People sat along the hallway.

51
00:02:45,925 --> 00:02:48,734
A child was having her face wiped by her mother.

52
00:02:49,084 --> 00:02:52,224
Staff pushed small kiosks aside to clear a path.

53
00:02:52,774 --> 00:02:56,424
I found a spot near the wall and took out my phone to try calling again.

54
00:02:56,974 --> 00:02:58,035
Still nothing.

55
00:02:58,585 --> 00:03:02,912
A staff member pushed a water cart past, telling everyone to take one bottle.

56
00:03:03,262 --> 00:03:06,236
I took one, and asked if she knew what was happening.

57
00:03:06,786 --> 00:03:08,064
She shook her head.

58
00:03:08,614 --> 00:03:09,892
"We're waiting too."

59
00:03:10,442 --> 00:03:11,618
I sat down.

60
00:03:11,968 --> 00:03:15,746
For a few minutes, I thought I could stay here until things became clearer.

61
00:03:16,296 --> 00:03:19,117
Then, somewhere upstairs, someone screamed.

62
00:03:19,667 --> 00:03:22,578
At first, only a few people stood up to look.

63
00:03:23,128 --> 00:03:26,778
Then someone came running down the escalator and fell right at the bottom.

64
00:03:27,128 --> 00:03:29,209
The person behind tripped over them.

65
00:03:29,559 --> 00:03:31,641
The screaming spread down the hallway.

66
00:03:32,191 --> 00:03:34,719
I stood up, trying to see the main entrance.

67
00:03:35,269 --> 00:03:38,090
People from the doors were now running back inside.

68
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:41,423
I didn't know which direction was more dangerous.

69
00:03:41,773 --> 00:03:45,602
When the people next to me surged toward the stairwell door, I went with them.

70
00:03:46,152 --> 00:03:49,012
We made it down one floor before the whole line stopped.

71
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:52,306
Below, someone was screaming not to push.

72
00:03:52,856 --> 00:03:55,320
But above, people kept pouring down.

73
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:57,914
I got pressed against the handrail.

74
00:03:58,264 --> 00:04:01,838
My backpack caught on something behind me, yanking my shoulder back.

75
00:04:02,188 --> 00:04:04,779
I turned, but there wasn't room to reach it.

76
00:04:05,329 --> 00:04:07,207
A man slammed into my back.

77
00:04:07,757 --> 00:04:08,537
"Move!"

78
00:04:09,087 --> 00:04:12,010
I tried to say I was stuck, but he wasn't listening.

79
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:16,364
I slipped one strap off my shoulder, reached back, and yanked hard.

80
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:18,808
The bag tore free from the railing.

81
00:04:19,158 --> 00:04:22,502
My hand scraped against a metal edge, and it stung badly.

82
00:04:23,052 --> 00:04:25,619
At the landing there was a door standing open.

83
00:04:25,969 --> 00:04:29,351
I squeezed past the person beside me and nearly fell through it.

84
00:04:29,901 --> 00:04:31,651
It was a staff corridor.

85
00:04:32,201 --> 00:04:37,203
I followed the arrows toward an exit, down a ramp, and pushed through a door into a loading area.

86
00:04:37,753 --> 00:04:41,072
Out here there were only trucks and crates stacked against the wall.

87
00:04:41,622 --> 00:04:43,921
I walked a few more steps and sat down.

88
00:04:44,471 --> 00:04:46,042
My hand was bleeding.

89
00:04:46,392 --> 00:04:51,305
I pressed a tissue against it, but my hand was shaking too hard, and I dropped the whole pack.

90
00:04:51,855 --> 00:04:55,824
I sat there for a moment before I could bring myself to bend down and pick it up.

91
00:04:56,374 --> 00:04:59,042
I drank a few sips of water and checked my phone.

92
00:04:59,592 --> 00:05:00,921
No missed calls.

93
00:05:01,471 --> 00:05:06,525
I wanted to go home, but every time I thought about the people out in the hallway, I stopped myself.

94
00:05:07,075 --> 00:05:10,279
Through the gap between two trucks, I could see the street.

95
00:05:10,629 --> 00:05:12,965
Someone ran past the mouth of the alley.

96
00:05:13,315 --> 00:05:16,621
Behind them, two others were walking, slow and steady.

97
00:05:17,171 --> 00:05:19,993
A car parked nearby started blaring its alarm.

98
00:05:20,543 --> 00:05:23,785
The two walking figures stopped, and turned toward the car.

99
00:05:24,335 --> 00:05:28,011
I watched them move to the door and slap their hands against the glass.

100
00:05:28,561 --> 00:05:32,020
From inside the mall, a fire alarm started ringing too.

101
00:05:32,370 --> 00:05:35,102
Someone near the end of the street turned around.

102
00:05:35,452 --> 00:05:36,526
Then another.

103
00:05:37,076 --> 00:05:38,443
I ducked down low.

104
00:05:38,993 --> 00:05:41,215
I didn't yet know what was wrong with them.

105
00:05:41,565 --> 00:05:44,220
But I had seen enough not to want to get closer.

106
00:05:44,770 --> 00:05:52,451
When the loading area went quiet, I tore a strip of fabric from a shirt in my backpack, wrapped it around my hand, and left through the alley at the back.

107
00:05:53,001 --> 00:05:55,452
I kept away from the direction of the ringing.

108
00:05:56,002 --> 00:05:58,645
By afternoon, I had been walking for hours.

109
00:05:59,195 --> 00:06:01,965
I finished off a snack bar and was still hungry.

110
00:06:02,315 --> 00:06:04,231
My feet had started to burn.

111
00:06:04,581 --> 00:06:07,849
I just wanted somewhere to sit down and some way to reach someone.

112
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:12,368
At the end of a row of houses, I found one with its door open a crack.

113
00:06:12,918 --> 00:06:14,885
I stood at the gate for a moment.

114
00:06:15,235 --> 00:06:17,316
No one in sight, no sound.

115
00:06:17,866 --> 00:06:19,565
I called out, softly.

116
00:06:20,115 --> 00:06:21,367
"Is anyone home?"

117
00:06:21,917 --> 00:06:23,042
No answer.

118
00:06:23,592 --> 00:06:25,444
There was a crack around the lock.

119
00:06:25,794 --> 00:06:30,465
I saw it, but told myself the owner might have damaged the door themselves on the way out.

120
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:33,403
I pushed the door open and stepped inside.

121
00:06:33,953 --> 00:06:35,651
The living room was empty.

122
00:06:36,001 --> 00:06:39,435
A chair had been knocked over, things scattered across the floor.

123
00:06:39,785 --> 00:06:42,581
A half-finished glass of water sat on the table.

124
00:06:43,131 --> 00:06:46,564
I had just passed the foot of the stairs when I heard a sound above.

125
00:06:47,114 --> 00:06:48,099
A footstep.

126
00:06:48,649 --> 00:06:49,659
I looked up.

127
00:06:50,209 --> 00:06:54,318
Someone was standing at the top of the stairs, half-hidden behind the railing.

128
00:06:54,868 --> 00:06:56,236
"Sorry," I said.

129
00:06:56,586 --> 00:06:57,723
"I just need—"

130
00:06:58,273 --> 00:07:00,240
The figure started coming down.

131
00:07:00,790 --> 00:07:03,420
I saw the blood on their shirt, then the face.

132
00:07:03,970 --> 00:07:07,136
I turned too fast and knocked into the table by the door.

133
00:07:07,486 --> 00:07:09,057
A vase fell and shattered.

134
00:07:09,607 --> 00:07:10,885
I ran outside.

135
00:07:11,435 --> 00:07:14,333
Not until the end of the street did I dare look back.

136
00:07:14,883 --> 00:07:19,464
The figure had reached the gate, standing in a patch of leftover sunlight on the sidewalk.

137
00:07:20,014 --> 00:07:23,830
I turned down a different alley and kept going until the house was out of sight.

138
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:28,362
When I finally stopped, I had to brace my hands on my knees just to breathe.

139
00:07:28,912 --> 00:07:31,491
I had seen the broken door before I went in.

140
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:33,587
I knew I shouldn't have.

141
00:07:34,137 --> 00:07:37,124
But I was tired, and I wanted that house to be empty.

142
00:07:37,674 --> 00:07:39,399
The light was starting to go.

143
00:07:39,949 --> 00:07:42,489
I had stopped looking for anywhere with a bed.

144
00:07:43,039 --> 00:07:46,371
The parking garage at the end of the street had its gate locked.

145
00:07:46,721 --> 00:07:49,491
I stood outside and looked in, called out once.

146
00:07:49,841 --> 00:07:50,966
No answer.

147
00:07:51,516 --> 00:07:53,827
I tried the apartment block next door.

148
00:07:54,177 --> 00:07:57,202
Just past the first flight of stairs, I smelled smoke.

149
00:07:57,552 --> 00:08:00,029
Somewhere above, an alarm kept ringing.

150
00:08:00,579 --> 00:08:01,755
I turned back.

151
00:08:02,305 --> 00:08:06,466
Behind a row of shops, I found a small building used for maintenance storage.

152
00:08:06,816 --> 00:08:09,242
A steel door, no windows on the wall.

153
00:08:09,592 --> 00:08:12,885
At the back, a low window opened onto a narrow yard.

154
00:08:13,435 --> 00:08:15,797
I walked around it before trying the handle.

155
00:08:16,347 --> 00:08:17,650
It wasn't locked.

156
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,716
I stood outside and called in, then waited.

157
00:08:21,266 --> 00:08:22,390
Nothing moved.

158
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:26,501
Inside were tool shelves, a few plastic bins, and a table.

159
00:08:26,851 --> 00:08:30,400
I switched on the flashlight and checked the blind corner behind the door.

160
00:08:30,950 --> 00:08:31,947
No one.

161
00:08:32,497 --> 00:08:36,441
The back window was wide enough to climb through if I set my bag down first.

162
00:08:36,791 --> 00:08:39,191
I tried the latch, then closed it again.

163
00:08:39,741 --> 00:08:41,797
Then I went back to the front door.

164
00:08:42,347 --> 00:08:43,765
The bolt still worked.

165
00:08:44,115 --> 00:08:46,758
I slid it shut, pulled on it twice to check.

166
00:08:47,308 --> 00:08:49,364
The room smelled of oil and dust.

167
00:08:49,714 --> 00:08:54,665
The concrete floor was cold, and there was nothing to lie on but a few flattened cardboard sheets.

168
00:08:55,215 --> 00:08:57,807
I laid them out against the wall and sat down.

169
00:08:58,357 --> 00:09:01,485
This time, before I ate, I looked back at the door.

170
00:09:02,035 --> 00:09:03,478
It was still closed.

171
00:09:04,028 --> 00:09:06,850
I finished the last snack bar and took out my phone.

172
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:08,780
No new messages.

173
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:11,096
Not a single bar of signal.

174
00:09:11,646 --> 00:09:14,302
I dimmed the screen and set it down beside me.

175
00:09:14,852 --> 00:09:16,627
I don't know when I fell asleep.

176
00:09:17,177 --> 00:09:19,399
A sound outside the door woke me up.

177
00:09:19,949 --> 00:09:23,178
I sat up fast and knocked the water bottle with my hand.

178
00:09:23,528 --> 00:09:27,880
It rolled off the cardboard, bounced on the floor, and hit the leg of a shelf.

179
00:09:28,430 --> 00:09:29,938
The sound wasn't loud.

180
00:09:30,488 --> 00:09:33,258
But right after, the footsteps outside stopped.

181
00:09:33,808 --> 00:09:35,226
I looked at the door.

182
00:09:35,776 --> 00:09:37,832
The handle moved, just slightly.

183
00:09:38,382 --> 00:09:39,749
Then came a push.

184
00:09:40,299 --> 00:09:42,661
I switched the flashlight on without thinking.

185
00:09:43,011 --> 00:09:45,170
The beam shook against the steel door.

186
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:46,908
Another push.

187
00:09:47,458 --> 00:09:49,795
I turned it off and backed against the wall.

188
00:09:50,145 --> 00:09:51,971
My heel scraped the floor.

189
00:09:52,521 --> 00:09:56,146
Outside, a scratching sound started right where I had been standing.

190
00:09:56,696 --> 00:09:57,872
I went still.

191
00:09:58,422 --> 00:10:00,478
The door rattled a few more times.

192
00:10:00,828 --> 00:10:05,511
The bolt held, but every sound of metal against metal made me think of the moment it wouldn't.

193
00:10:06,061 --> 00:10:08,653
I wanted to drag the table over to brace it.

194
00:10:09,203 --> 00:10:11,769
But the table was on the other side of the room.

195
00:10:12,119 --> 00:10:16,025
I remembered the bottle rolling, and the footsteps stopping right after.

196
00:10:16,375 --> 00:10:17,589
I didn't get up.

197
00:10:18,139 --> 00:10:22,095
I sat against the wall, arms around my knees, trying to breathe slowly.

198
00:10:22,645 --> 00:10:24,778
The noise outside went on for a while.

199
00:10:25,328 --> 00:10:27,090
Then it began to thin out.

200
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:30,003
I didn't know how many of them were out there.

201
00:10:30,353 --> 00:10:33,608
I didn't know if they had left, or were just standing, waiting.

202
00:10:34,158 --> 00:10:37,451
When my legs went numb, I still didn't dare stretch them out.

203
00:10:38,001 --> 00:10:41,945
Much later, there was the sound of glass breaking, somewhere in the distance.

204
00:10:42,494 --> 00:10:44,487
The footsteps outside shifted.

205
00:10:44,837 --> 00:10:48,474
The drag of their feet on the concrete grew fainter, then disappeared.

206
00:10:49,024 --> 00:10:52,164
I waited a long time before I reached for the water bottle.

207
00:10:52,714 --> 00:10:55,191
This time, I held it with both hands.

208
00:10:55,741 --> 00:10:58,422
Near dawn, I managed to sleep a little more.

209
00:10:58,972 --> 00:11:03,426
When I woke, my neck was so stiff I had to turn my whole body just to look behind me.

210
00:11:03,976 --> 00:11:07,065
I cracked open the back window and looked down at the yard.

211
00:11:07,615 --> 00:11:08,804
No one there.

212
00:11:09,354 --> 00:11:12,099
I had a bit more than one bottle of water left.

213
00:11:12,449 --> 00:11:13,803
The food was gone.

214
00:11:14,153 --> 00:11:17,013
My hand was faintly swollen under the dirty wrap.

215
00:11:17,363 --> 00:11:21,562
I needed to wash it, needed to eat, and needed to know where I actually was.

216
00:11:22,112 --> 00:11:24,270
There was still no reply on my phone.

217
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:28,432
I was about to try calling again when a new notification appeared.

218
00:11:28,982 --> 00:11:30,464
Evacuation point.

219
00:11:30,814 --> 00:11:33,138
River Crossing Bridge, north bank.

220
00:11:33,488 --> 00:11:35,352
Receiving until twelve noon.

221
00:11:35,902 --> 00:11:37,665
I read the address again.

222
00:11:38,215 --> 00:11:41,814
Yesterday I had walked into the mall because I saw a guard at the door.

223
00:11:42,164 --> 00:11:45,993
Now I was about to head toward a place that might be just as full of people.

224
00:11:46,543 --> 00:11:50,066
I sat there a little longer, looking at the bottle in my hand.

225
00:11:50,616 --> 00:11:54,088
If I stayed here, I would still have to go outside by noon anyway.

226
00:11:54,638 --> 00:11:58,926
I saved the evacuation address, in case the phone lost signal on the way.

227
00:11:59,476 --> 00:12:03,585
Then I put on the backpack, checked my pocket to make sure the phone was still there.

228
00:12:04,135 --> 00:12:06,332
Outside, footsteps passed by.

229
00:12:06,882 --> 00:12:09,346
I put my hand on the bolt, and waited.

230
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:13,355
Only when I couldn't hear anything anymore did I open the door.
